WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.200
-Guys, today is Friday
and that's usually when I

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:02.901
catch up on some personal stuff.

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:03.934
I check my inbox,

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:04.701
I return some emails,

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:05.534
and, of course, I send out

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:06.400
thank-you notes.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.267
And I was just running

00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:08.601
a bit behind today. I thought,

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:09.567
if you guys wouldn't mind,

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:10.400
I'd like to write out my weekly

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.467
thank-you notes right now.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:12.400
Is that okay with you guys?

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.901
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:17.467
Appreciate that.
Thank you.

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:19.901
James, can I get some thank-you
note writing music, please?

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:21.133
[ Playing tender tune ]

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:22.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:24.501
-Last week, he was smiling
from ear to ear.

00:00:24.501 --> 00:00:27.033
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:28.133
♪♪

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.067
Thank you, spring allergies,

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:32.234
for basically saying,
"You can have nice weather

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:35.067
or you can breathe,
but you can't have both."

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:37.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:38.234
Now, behave.

00:00:40.701 --> 00:00:41.801
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.801 --> 00:00:43.267
Thank you, Easter,

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:44.934
for being
the second-best holiday

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:47.100
where a magical person breaks
in to your house.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:51.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:51.734 --> 00:00:53.667
It's the second-best holiday
where a stranger --

00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:56.100
a magical someone breaks in.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.467
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.467 --> 00:00:59.901
Thank you, Easter Bunny,
for always dressing

00:00:59.901 --> 00:01:01.901
like a blackjack dealer
at Chuck E. Cheese.

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:04.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:06.501 --> 00:01:09.501
-22.
-Good luck.

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:10.667
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:13.167
Thank you, New York City's
steam pipes,

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:16.000
for looks like Sixth Avenue
is celebrating 4/20 early.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:20.767
My corner is vaping.

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:24.901
♪♪

00:01:24.901 --> 00:01:27.968
Thank you, filing taxes
as a single person,

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:30.000
for being that time of year
you tell the government

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.868
you biffed it
on the dating apps.

00:01:31.868 --> 00:01:34.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:35.767
Tried.

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:39.667
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:42.000
Thank you, napkin dispensers,

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.601
for always giving me
two options --

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:45.300
one napkin or 600.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:47.534 --> 00:01:49.067
I'll take a pile.

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:49.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.601 --> 00:01:53.634
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:54.767
Thank you,

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:56.934
putting pennies
in a mall fountain,

00:01:56.934 --> 00:01:59.133
because, if there's anywhere
my wish will come true,

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:01.133
it's between Hot Topic
and Cinnabon.

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:04.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:08.968 --> 00:02:10.300
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.934
Thank you, quiche,
or as I like to call you,

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:14.701
egg pie.
There you have it, everybody.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:15.968
[ Cheering and applause ]
Those are our "Thank You Notes."

